Java Bean Class Student
Question 1
Create a Java Bean class Student with the following fields:

roll: Integer
name: String
age: Integer
marks: Integer
Make sure that encapsulation is maintained. Make validation checks before setting the age
and marks of the Student (i.e., are they in the valid range, 18 < age < 60, 0 < marks < 500).


Inside a separate class main method, create 2 objects of the Student class: one by using the
zero-argument constructor and the second by using the parameterized constructor. Print the
details of both the Student objects.